---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import DiscoveryField from '../components/DiscoveryField.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Next Motion AI"
  description="Next Motion AI explores how reinforcement learning can guide discovery in computational biology."
>
  <main id="main-content">
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="container hero-grid">
        <div class="hero-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-line"></span> REINFORCEMENT LEARNING FOR COMPUTATIONAL BIOLOGY</p>
          <h1>Building a discovery engine for biology.</h1>
          <p class="hero-description">We’re exploring how reinforcement learning can help navigate biological design spaces, learn from feedback, and reveal promising directions for scientific study.</p>
          <div class="hero-actions">
            <a class="button button-dark" href="/docs/who_we_are">Explore our approach <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
            <a class="text-link" href="mailto:contact@nextmotionai.com">Get in touch <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <DiscoveryField />
      </div>
      <div class="container hero-footnote"><span>01 / AN OPEN FIELD OF DISCOVERY</span><span>SCROLL TO EXPLORE ↓</span></div>
    </section>

    <section class="thesis-section section-space" aria-labelledby="thesis-heading">
      <div class="container thesis-grid">
        <p class="eyebrow section-kicker"><span class="eyebrow-line"></span> THE IDEA</p>
        <div>
          <h2 id="thesis-heading" class="display-heading">Biology is full of possibilities. <em>Finding the right ones is the challenge.</em></h2>
          <p class="section-lede">Useful designs may depend on combinations, constraints, and tradeoffs that are difficult to assess one by one. We’re interested in methods that can search more deliberately and learn from each step.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="approach-section section-space" aria-labelledby="approach-heading">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-heading-row">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-line"></span> OUR RESEARCH LENS</p>
            <h2 id="approach-heading" class="display-heading">A smarter way to <em>explore.</em></h2>
          </div>
          <p>Reinforcement learning offers a way to think about discovery as an iterative process: make a choice, observe feedback, and decide what to explore next.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="lens-grid">
          <article class="lens-card">
            <span class="lens-number">01 <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span>
            <svg class="lens-art" viewBox="0 0 280 112" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><g fill="none" stroke="#779e9b" stroke-width="1.4"><path d="M28 93V22h224v71H28Z" stroke-dasharray="3 6"/><path d="M55 76V39h170v37H55Z"/><path d="M79 65V50h122v15H79Z"/></g><path d="M107 57h66" stroke="#397e8b" stroke-width="2"/><circle cx="140" cy="57" r="11" fill="#e2f0e8" stroke="#397e8b" stroke-width="2"/><circle cx="140" cy="57" r="3" fill="#397e8b"/></svg>
            <h3>Frame the question</h3>
            <p>Start with the biological objective and the constraints that make a useful answer meaningful.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="lens-card">
            <span class="lens-number">02 <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span>
            <svg class="lens-art" viewBox="0 0 280 112" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><g fill="none" stroke="#779e9b" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M23 90c48-5 69-34 104-37 44-4 67 31 130 11"/><path d="M23 90c55 8 67-9 110-3 43 6 70-15 124-47"/><path d="M23 90c40-24 69-13 94-44 34-43 74-27 140-21"/></g><path d="M23 90c40-24 69-13 94-44 34-43 74-27 140-21" fill="none" stroke="#3c8391" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"/><g fill="#f8faf5" stroke="#3c8391" stroke-width="2"><circle cx="23" cy="90" r="5"/><circle cx="117" cy="46" r="5"/><circle cx="257" cy="25" r="5"/></g></svg>
            <h3>Explore possibilities</h3>
            <p>Consider how an adaptive search might navigate a space too large to examine exhaustively.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="lens-card">
            <span class="lens-number">03 <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span>
            <svg class="lens-art" viewBox="0 0 280 112" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M50 69c8-30 31-45 57-45 43 0 47 63 92 63 25 0 40-16 42-40" fill="none" stroke="#779e9b" stroke-width="1.5"/><path d="M49 70c-1 20 16 25 37 23 24-2 40-24 59-42 22-21 48-32 79-16" fill="none" stroke="#3c8391" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"/><g fill="#f8faf5" stroke="#3c8391" stroke-width="2"><circle cx="49" cy="70" r="5"/><circle cx="145" cy="51" r="5"/><circle cx="224" cy="35" r="5"/></g><path d="m219 31 7 4-7 4" fill="none" stroke="#3c8391" stroke-width="1.5"/></svg>
            <h3>Learn from feedback</h3>
            <p>Use each observation to inform the next question, while remaining clear about what the evidence can show.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
        <a class="text-link approach-link" href="/docs/who_we_are">More about our approach <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="evidence-section section-space" aria-labelledby="evidence-heading">
      <svg class="evidence-art" viewBox="0 0 570 570" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><g fill="none" stroke="#9bc9bd" stroke-opacity=".25" stroke-width="1"><path d="M-42 284C-42 130 94 0 285 0S612 130 612 284 476 568 285 568-42 438-42 284Z"/><path d="M-7 284C-7 145 116 35 285 35s292 110 292 249-123 249-292 249S-7 423-7 284Z"/><path d="M28 284C28 161 138 70 285 70s257 91 257 214-110 214-257 214S28 407 28 284Z"/><path d="M63 284C63 177 160 105 285 105s222 72 222 179-97 179-222 179S63 391 63 284Z"/><path d="M98 284c0-91 84-144 187-144s187 53 187 144-84 144-187 144S98 375 98 284Z"/><path d="M133 284c0-75 72-109 152-109s152 34 152 109-72 109-152 109-152-34-152-109Z"/><path d="M168 284c0-59 60-74 117-74s117 15 117 74-60 74-117 74-117-15-117-74Z"/></g><path d="M15 432c91-82 150-98 225-92 75 6 156-52 274-216" fill="none" stroke="#a9dace" stroke-opacity=".55" stroke-width="2"/><circle cx="240" cy="340" r="7" fill="#b1dfd1"/></svg>
      <div class="container evidence-grid">
        <p class="eyebrow eyebrow-light"><span class="eyebrow-line"></span> BUILT ON CURIOSITY, GROUNDED IN EVIDENCE</p>
        <div>
          <h2 id="evidence-heading">Good questions need <em>good evidence.</em></h2>
          <p>Computational ideas are a starting point for discovery. Careful comparisons, reproducible work, and honest limits are how we learn whether an approach is useful.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="contact-section section-space" aria-labelledby="contact-heading">
      <div class="container contact-grid">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-line"></span> START A CONVERSATION</p>
          <h2 id="contact-heading" class="display-heading">Let’s explore what’s <em>possible.</em></h2>
        </div>
        <div class="contact-action">
          <p>Interested in the intersection of reinforcement learning and biology? We’d like to hear from you.</p>
          <a class="button button-dark" href="mailto:contact@nextmotionai.com">Get in touch <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
